{"nodes": [{"id": "index_page", "label": "Conecta Yungay \u2014 Index Page", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "index_content_security_policy", "label": "Content Security Policy (Frontend Security Layer)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "GitHub Pages hosting does not allow configuring HTTP headers, so security controls must work purely via <meta> tags or JS. The CSP meta tag whitelists only unpkg.com (Leaflet), cdnjs.cloudflare.com (html2canvas), and Google Fonts domains, and blocks inline scripts, other origins, objects and iframes. 'unsafe-inline' is kept in style-src only because Leaflet applies styles inline via JS. frame-ancestors (anti-clickjacking) cannot be set via <meta>, so that protection is explicitly noted as limited on GitHub Pages.", "source_file": "index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "index_https_enforcement", "label": "Forced HTTPS Redirect", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "HTTPS is enforced via an external script (js/httpsRedirect.js) rather than an inline script specifically so the CSP does not need to allow 'unsafe-inline' for script-src.", "source_file": "index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "index_layered_architecture", "label": "N-Layer Script Loading Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Scripts are loaded in an explicit dependency order: security (securityUtils.js) first because other modules depend on Security.escapeHTML, then data layer (routeRepository.js, surveyCatalogs.js, surveyRepository.js), then business layer (routeService.js, visitService.js), then presentation layer (mapRenderer.js, surveyPanel.js, uiController.js).", "source_file": "index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_